## 3. Kubernetes Configuration

File: `nginx-phpfpm.yaml`

### 3.1 ConfigMap — Nginx Configuration

The ConfigMap stores the custom Nginx configuration.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: nginx-config
data:
  nginx.conf: |
    events {
        worker_connections 1024;
    }

    http {
        include /etc/nginx/mime.types;
        default_type application/octet-stream;

        server {
            listen 8093;
            server_name localhost;

            root /var/www/html;
            index index.html index.htm index.php;

            location / {
                try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
            }

            location ~ \.php$ {
                try_files $uri =404;
                fastcgi_pass 127.0.0.1:9000;
                fastcgi_index index.php;
                include fastcgi_params;
                fastcgi_param SCRIPT_FILENAME $document_root$fastcgi_script_name;
            }
        }
    }
```

**Important configuration details:**

- Nginx listens on port `8093`.
- The document root is `/var/www/html`.
- PHP files are processed through PHP-FPM on port `9000`.
- The index directive supports HTML and PHP index files.

### 3.2 Pod — Nginx and PHP-FPM

The Pod contains two containers sharing the same application directory.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: nginx-phpfpm
  labels:
    app: nginx-phpfpm
spec:
  containers:
    - name: nginx-container
      image: nginx:latest
      ports:
        - containerPort: 8093
          protocol: TCP
      volumeMounts:
        - name: shared-files
          mountPath: /var/www/html
        - name: nginx-config-volume
          mountPath: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
          subPath: nginx.conf
          readOnly: true

    - name: php-fpm-container
      image: php:8.1-fpm-alpine
      ports:
        - containerPort: 9000
          protocol: TCP
      volumeMounts:
        - name: shared-files
          mountPath: /var/www/html

  volumes:
    - name: shared-files
      emptyDir: {}
    - name: nginx-config-volume
      configMap:
        name: nginx-config
```

**Key implementation details:**

- Both containers mount `shared-files` at `/var/www/html`.
- The `emptyDir` volume allows both containers to access the same application files.
- The ConfigMap is mounted into the Nginx container as `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf`.
- The `subPath` setting mounts the `nginx.conf` key as a file.
- Nginx communicates with PHP-FPM using `127.0.0.1:9000`, because both containers run inside the same Pod.

### 3.3 NodePort Service

The Service exposes Nginx through Kubernetes NodePort `30012`.

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: nginx-phpfpm
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: nginx-phpfpm
  ports:
    - name: http
      protocol: TCP
      port: 8093
      targetPort: 8093
      nodePort: 30012
```

## 4. Deployment Instructions

Run the following commands from the Kubernetes Jump Host.

### Step 1: Create the project directory

```bash
mkdir -p ~/nginx-phpfpm
cd ~/nginx-phpfpm
```

### Step 2: Confirm the PHP application file exists

```bash
ls -l /opt/index.php
```

### Step 3: Validate the Kubernetes manifest

```bash
kubectl apply --dry-run=client -f nginx-phpfpm.yaml
```

### Step 4: Deploy the resources

```bash
kubectl apply -f nginx-phpfpm.yaml
```

### Step 5: Verify the Pod, ConfigMap and Service

```bash
kubectl get pods
kubectl get configmap nginx-config
kubectl get svc nginx-phpfpm
```

### Step 6: Copy the PHP application into the Nginx container

```bash
kubectl cp /opt/index.php \
  nginx-phpfpm:/var/www/html/index.php \
  -c nginx-container
```

### Step 7: Verify the shared volume

Check the file inside the Nginx container:

```bash
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm \
  -c nginx-container -- \
  ls -l /var/www/html/index.php
```

Check the same file inside PHP-FPM:

```bash
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm \
  -c php-fpm-container -- \
  ls -l /var/www/html/index.php
```

### Step 8: Validate Nginx configuration

```bash
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm \
  -c nginx-container -- nginx -t
```

### Step 9: Test application access

Port-forward the Kubernetes Service:

```bash
kubectl port-forward svc/nginx-phpfpm 18093:8093
```

In a second terminal, execute:

```bash
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:18093/
```

